~ start

# Sync the CANS derived skill for the roll in splice_nyx:
# roll bonus = live can percentage × 0.6 (100% cans → +60 points).
do Skills.sync_cans_from_pct(60.0)

if GameState.get_flag("refused_splice", false)
	=> already_refused

if GameState.get_flag("betrayed_friends", false)
	=> already_committed

Splice: Easy. Easy.
do Cutscene.show_video("res://cutscenes/splice_intro.ogv")
Splice: The trap was for the conversation. That's all.
Splice: Splice. You may have heard the name.
Splice: I've been on your signal since the first run. You didn't know. That was the point.
Splice: You're better at this than the crew you came in with realizes. They've got you running their little chores.
Splice: Step off-channel a minute. Just listen. Walk away if you want.
- Get off my channel. [#exit]
	=> splice_refused
- Listening.
	=> splice_consider
- [CANS 0%] What about Nyx? [if not GameState.get_flag("splice_nyx_door_rolled", false) /]
	=> splice_nyx_roll

~ splice_consider

# Read by dial_tone's post-3 debrief ("Bitter. World-rigged...") — that
# option only exists if the player actually sat through the pitch.
do GameState.set_flag("splice_pitched", true)
Splice: Here's what nobody on that channel will tell you.
Splice: The grid was never **free**!
Splice: DialTone runs it. The way he ran you.
Splice: Picks his runner. Writes the story.
Splice: Keeps the rest of the **sheeple** chasing soda cans like it matters.
Splice: I **was** them once. I **left** because I figured it out.
Splice: Walk with me, you don't grind anymore. The Gibson responds when you blink. Sentinels, routing, the whole stack — yours.
Splice: You didn't grab it. You saw it. DialTone's crew is still playing make-believe.
=> splice_hub

# HUB — menu only, no monologue. Every probe loops back HERE, not to
# splice_consider, so the sheeple pitch above plays exactly once.

~ splice_hub

- They say you will destroy the Gibson.
	Splice: It's not destruction. It's just **monetization**.
	Splice: If I don't do it someone else will. This is just the way the world works.
	Splice: DialTone's going to come to the same conclusion in about a month.
	Splice: Just wait.
	=> splice_hub
- What's the catch?
	=> splice_catch
- [CANS 0%] What about Nyx? [if not GameState.get_flag("splice_nyx_door_rolled", false) /]
	=> splice_nyx_roll
- I'm with you. [#exit]
	=> splice_committed
- Get off my channel. [#exit]
	=> splice_refused

~ splice_catch

Splice: There isn't one. That's what they don't get.
Splice: They built the "hackers for the people" thing because none of them had anything worth keeping.
Splice: You're the same. That's why I'm talking to you and not them.
- And if I say no?
	=> splice_if_no
- I'm in. [#exit]
	=> splice_committed
- Get off my channel. [#exit]
	=> splice_refused

~ splice_if_no

Splice: Then you go back to your soda run and your little prank crew. No hard feelings.
Splice: You'll think about this. Probably tonight.
Splice: When you do — channel's open.
- Actually, I'm in. [#exit]
	=> splice_committed
- Get off my channel. [#exit]
	=> splice_refused

# CHECK — cans-driven door roll (0 base + can% × 0.6, clamp floors it at
# 5%). Always visible until rolled so the player sees the odds they're
# carrying — a missed door is a visible miss, not a silent one. Shared by
# both menus above; one roll total, pass opens the splice_nyx sub-hub.

~ splice_nyx_roll

do GameState.set_flag("splice_nyx_door_rolled", true)
if Skills.roll("cans", 0)
	=> splice_nyx
Splice: Nyx.
Splice: No.
Splice: We're here to talk about **you**.
=> splice_hub

~ splice_nyx

# Read by dial_tone's post-3 debrief ("It got personal. About Nyx.") —
# that option only exists if Splice actually went here.
do GameState.set_flag("splice_mentioned_nyx", true)
Splice: yeah.
Splice: I pitched the same thing to her. She almost ran with it... almost.
Splice: she -
Splice: She's not part of this conversation, runner.
Splice: Some things I keep mine.
- "Almost"?
	Splice: Long time ago. Doesn't matter.
	=> splice_hub
# CHECK — cans-driven roll (30% base + can% × 0.6). One-shot; pushes into
# the sentence Splice cut off at "she -". Pass ties to dial_tone's backdoor
# thread ("He found a backdoor. / He made one.") — Nyx burned it on sight.
- [CANS 30%] You were about to say something else. [if not GameState.get_flag("splice_nyx_rolled", false) /]
	do GameState.set_flag("splice_nyx_rolled", true)
	if Skills.roll("cans", 30)
		Splice: ...fine.
		Splice: She found my backdoor before it was finished. Burned it within the hour. No warning. No goodbye.
		Splice: She's as straightlaced as they come.
	else
		Splice: No.
		Splice: You get the pitch, runner. You don't get **me**.
	=> splice_hub
- [if GameState.coin_pct() >= 0.8 /] [CAN] Are you trying to get her back?
	Splice: I'm trying to get the Gibson. Nyx made her call a long time ago.
	=> splice_hub
- Get off my channel. [#exit]
	=> splice_refused

~ splice_committed

Splice: There it is. Knew you'd see it.
Splice: Walk with me, {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}.
Splice: I think we are going to be great friends.
do GameState.set_flag("betrayed_friends", true)
do Audio.resume_default_playlist_if_overridden()
do LevelProgression.goto_path("res://level/level_5.tscn")
=> END

~ splice_refused

Splice: ...wow. [sighs] Wow okay. [#model=eleven_v3]
Splice: You're not walking out of here, runner.
Splice: Those power-ups in your pocket? They're **keys**. They unlock the whole sector — you don't even know what.
Splice: So I'm taking them. Every one. Then I'm deleting the part of the wire that has **you** on it.
Splice: Hold still. This is the —
Splice: Wait.
Splice: What — what's happening?
Splice: My access — my access is —
Splice: **No**. No no **NO**!
DialTone: Got him. Go go go. [#walkie]
Nyx: {{HandlePicker.chosen_name()}}, you've got a window. We can't hold this. **Run**. [#walkie]
Splice: I'll find you again. I will **find you**, runner.
Nyx: Go. Now. [#walkie]
do GameState.set_flag("refused_splice", true)
do Audio.resume_default_playlist_if_overridden()
do LevelProgression.advance()
=> END

~ already_refused

Splice: We're done talking, runner.
=> END

~ already_committed

Splice: I told you not to move.
=> END
